From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Amity Square's maps sent by their cells in the view
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Amity Square's four maps have big models (14,000 vertices between them),
and by the lake in its middle all four are partly in the view: each was
sent whole, every vertex worked out, and the 3D's core took 33 ms a scene
there (45 frames a second, a log of 2026-11-07).

In the matrices listed (sPortCelledMatrices: Amity Square) a loaded map
is sent with only its cells in the view (Port_RenderMapCells): its
polygons by the 8 by 8 tile cell their middle is in, each cell's part of
each shape's list cut out once (two shapes a scene, the whole map sent
meanwhile). Each scene a cell is in the view if both its column and its
row are (the DS's box test, the model's box set to theirs), each shape's
list is made of those cells' parts again only when they change, and the
model is drawn once. A shape whose parts take the colour, normal or
texture coordinates from one another (sent in another order, they'd take
the wrong ones) is sent whole; none in Amity Square.

On the PC the same pictures; by the lake 15.0 to 16.0k vertices a scene
to 7.7 to 10.0k, and the game's thread a little quicker there too (fewer
vertices sent).
---
